+### §stable-tab-keys — closing a tab renumbers the others (overridden)
+- Since: 2026-10-23 (supersedes the 2026-09-02 decision; user overrode it on 2026-10-23)
+- Decision: closing a tab renumbers the remaining tabs so keys stay contiguous (`t1,t2,t3`), and `next` is reset to the tab count + 1.
+- Previously: keys were assigned once and never shifted, leaving gaps (`t1,t3`). That was forbidden-to-change until the maintainer explicitly overrode it.
+- Known cost (from the superseded record): the key is the React key and the URL state, so shifting keys remounts every tab to the right of the closed one and drops its scroll position and unsaved form input (incident 2026-08-29). Accepted by the maintainer.
 - Evidence: `tab-keys.test.mjs`
